# expect: expected `,` or `]`, found `b`
# A newline separates list elements (spec §4.11); nothing else was added. Two
# elements on one line still need the comma, and juxtaposition is not a
# separator. The element ends at the first token that cannot continue it, and a
# name standing there on the same line is reported as the missing comma it is
# (#190); the parser then reads `b` as the next element. Recorded because
# "the commas are optional" is the sentence a reader will carry away from the
# multi-line form, and this is the half of it that is not true.
fn f(a: Int, b: Int) -> List[Int] = [a b]
